quota workspace can be tidied up. Gate WHOLE operations at their boundary — a folder copy, `replace`, staging a run's inputs all check once up front (`ensure_room_for`) because a gate in the middle of a loop leaves half of it applied; `move` is exempt (net-zero) and `write_record` is exempt (it records an effect that ALREADY happened — refusing it only makes the re-run repeat the side effects). There is no second size cap — a size-based reaper was capacity management dressed as a policy limit, and idle reap already reclaims the whole item dir, `.home` included. A turn is refused OUTRIGHT when the workspace is already full (`chat_send.send` / `workflow_exec.drive_turn`, before the user's message is persisted): gating each write still let the agent burn a turn rediscovering it, and clearing space needs no agent because deleting is never gated.
